  "claim": "The writer/director/actor from Glen or Glenda has the career titles actor, writer, producer, and director. The director of Cyrano de Bergerac (1946 film) also has the career titles actor, writer, producer, and director.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Ed Wood. Sentence: Edward Davis Wood Jr. (October 10, 1924 – December 10, 1978) was an American filmmaker, actor, writer, producer, and director.\nPage: Fernand Rivers. Sentence: Fernand Rivers (born François Large, 6 September 1879, Saint-Lager - 12 September 1960) was a French actor, screenwriter, film producer and director.\nPage: Glen or Glenda. Sentence: Glen or Glenda is a 1953 American drama film written, directed by and starring Ed Wood (credited in his starring role as \"Daniel Davis\"), and featuring Bela Lugosi and Wood's then-girlfriend Dolores Fuller.\nPage: Cyrano de Bergerac (1946 film). Sentence: Cyrano de Bergerac is a 1946 French romantic comedy film directed by Fernand Rivers and starring Claude Dauphin, Ellen Bernsen and Pierre Bertin.",
