        "original_id": "258ed7e0-81ad-51e2-a701-3c9ba2e6e4d6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ed Wood, Fernand Rivers, Bela Lugosi, Dolores Fuller, Claude Dauphin, Ellen Bernsen, Pierre Bertin\n- Films: Glen or Glenda, Cyrano de Bergerac (1946 film)\n- Roles: filmmaker, actor, writer, producer, director, screenwriter\n\nFacts:\n- Fernand Rivers was born François Large on 6 September 1879 in Saint-Lager and died on 12 September 1960.\n- Fernand Rivers was a French actor, screenwriter, film producer, and director.\n- Cyrano de Bergerac is a 1946 French romantic comedy film directed by Fernand Rivers and starring Claude Dauphin, Ellen Bernsen, and Pierre Bertin.\n- Ed Wood was born Edward Davis Wood Jr. on October 10, 1924, and died on December 10, 1978.\n- Ed Wood was an American filmmaker, actor, writer, producer, and director.\n- Glen or Glenda is a 1953 American drama film written, directed by, and starring Ed Wood, who was credited in the starring role as Daniel Davis.\n- Glen or Glenda features Bela Lugosi and Ed Wood's then-girlfriend Dolores Fuller.",
